-- title:
--   Primes of O[B] over mathfrak m_O are maximal
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field and let $A_0$ be a domain which is a discrete valuation ring, equipped with an algebra map to $F$. Let $O$ be a subring of $F$ whose underlying ring is local and Noetherian, and assume the image of $A_0$ in $F$ is contained in $O$ and that every element of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ maps into the maximal ideal of $O$. Let $B$ be a finitely generated $A_0$-subalgebra of $F$, and assume: for every prime ideal $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ which contains the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ under $A_0 \to B$ and which is not maximal, there is a valuation subring $V$ of $F$ whose elements are exactly the $f \in F$ with $f c = b$ for some $b, c \in B$ with $c \notin \mathfrak q$ (so $V$ is the localisation $B_{\mathfrak q}$ taken inside $F$), and $V$ fails to dominate $O$, in the sense that it is not the case that both $O \subseteq V$ and every element of the maximal ideal of $O$ is a non-unit of $V$. Finally let $\mathfrak R$ be a prime ideal of the $O$-subalgebra $O[B]$ of $F$ generated by $B$, and suppose an element $g$ of $O$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O$ if and only if its image in $O[B]$ lies in $\mathfrak R$. Then $\mathfrak R$ is a maximal ideal.
--
--   The assertion is that, under the stated hypothesis ruling out contracted (non-maximal) components, the fibre of $\operatorname{Spec} O[B] \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ over the closed point is zero-dimensional; it is a step in the Zariski main theorem circle of ideas used to realise a local ring as a localisation of an affine model. It is invoked by [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_localRing_eq_localization_of_affineModel_of_map_maximalIdeal_le_of_isIntegrallyClosed_ofPrime`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_localRing_eq_localization_of_affineModel_of_map_maximalIdeal_le_of_isIntegrallyClosed_ofPrime) and by [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_localRing_eq_localization_of_normal_affineModel_of_map_maximalIdeal_le`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_localRing_eq_localization_of_normal_affineModel_of_map_maximalIdeal_le), and its proof uses [`ValuationSubring.eq_or_eq_top_of_toSubring_le_of_isDiscreteValuationRing`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.eq_or_eq_top_of_toSubring_le_of_isDiscreteValuationRing), the statement that a subring of $F$ containing a valuation subring which is a discrete valuation ring is either that subring or all of $F$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Subring_isMaximal_of_liesOver_adjoin_of_forall_not_isMaximal_valuationSubring.lean

